    9573/    F466 :                     	; In a rather overzealous optimisation, this game doesn't check if
    9574/    F466 :                     	; the sprite limit has been reached every time it processes a sprite
    9575/    F466 :                     	; piece. Naturally, this leads to the 'Sprite_Table' buffer being
    9576/    F466 :                     	; overflowed if too many sprites are processed. To mitigate this, the
    9577/    F466 :                     	; developers placed an $80 byte large spill buffer after
    9578/    F466 :                     	; 'Sprite_Table', to 'catch' the overflow. Unfortunately, this spill
    9579/    F466 :                     	; buffer is not big enough to catch all overflow: this oversight is
    9580/    F466 :                     	; responsible for the famous 'Ashua' bug. To fix this, we'll just
    9581/    F466 :                     	; undo this optimistaion. Sonic 3 & Knuckles undid this optimistaion
    9582/    F466 :                     	; too, but heavily optimised the rest of 'BuildSprites' to make up
    9583/    F466 :                     	; for it.
