   10881/   11016 :                     		; We now perform the y portion of a bounding box check.  To do this, we assume a
   10882/   11016 :                     		; coordinate system where the y origin is at the highest y position relative to the object
   10883/   11016 :                     		; at which Sonic would still collide with it.  This point is
   10884/   11016 :                     		;   y_pos(object) - width(object)/2 - y_radius(Sonic) - 4,
   10885/   11016 :                     		; where object is stored in (a0), Sonic in (a1), and height(object)/2 in d2.  This way
   10886/   11016 :                     		; of doing it causes the object's hitbox to be vertically off-center by -4 pixels.
